--- stdout
[1mExemptions[0m — what a package registers to quiet a general rule (by slug or class).

  [36marray-callback-contract[0m The framework requires this method's callback to return an array.
  [36marray-callback-input-contract[0m The framework supplies an array to this method's callback.
  [36marray-input-contract[0m This framework boundary takes arrays carrying values in its declared input format.
  [36marray-return-contract[0m The framework requires this hook to return an array.
  [36marray-returning [0m A class whose whole job is handing the framework arrays (a FormRequest, an MCP tool) — its array returns are contractual, exempt from array-return-bag (class-level).
  [36massociation     [0m A call or attribute declaring one end of a two-way association (an ORM relation like `hasOne(Picker::class)`, a binding like `#[ObservedBy(OrderObserver::class)]`) — the framework requires both ends to name each other, so the reference carries no dependency direction and cannot close a cycle.
  [36mboundary        [0m A framework entry point (an HTTP/RPC request) — exempt from feature-envy (don't move behaviour onto it) and pass-the-object (a method taking one may unpack its input).
  [36mcomposition-root[0m A provider or framework construction hook that wires config into values without constructor injection.
  [36mcontract-method [0m A framework-mandated method (`rules`/`schema`/`casts`/`Guard::user`/`Arrayable::toArray`) whose signature the framework dictates — exempt from near-duplicate, array-return-bag and de-nulled-finder.
  [36mcontrol-signal  [0m A Throwable thrown purely to steer control flow, not to report a failure (an engine's break/stop signal) — catching it with an empty body IS the semantics, so it is exempt from swallow-catch.
  [36mdynamic-members [0m A type whose framework supplies members at runtime, such as an Eloquent model with database attributes and query methods.
  [36mno-container    [0m A type the framework instantiates itself, no container/DI (an Eloquent cast, a Spatie DataPipe/Cast) — a loose array parameter and per-call container reach are the framework's convention; exempt from array-bag and container-reach.
  [36mvalidation-response[0m A framework factory builds a validation response from field messages and has no parameter for the caught failure.

[2mRun `commandments exemptions <sin|detector>` to see one detector's exemptions.[0m

